//? Title: Comb Sort: Gaps, Actual Work and Unstable Identities
//? Subtitle: The original seven integers and seed-four experiment, with exact gap arithmetic and a named bubble baseline
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Sorting a sequence by adjacent forward exchanges can leave a small value moving
left only one position per scan. Comb sort permits distant exchanges first,
then finishes with adjacent scans. We retain the original seven integers and
the seed-four, forty-size shuffle experiment, using actual counters from the
native sorting kernels. The report distinguishes measured comparison savings
from an asymptotic guarantee, identifies the original full-width bubble baseline,
and shows that already sorted input still traverses the wide gaps. Carried
original identities expose instability even though equal keys never swap directly.
Gap arithmetic is exact for the complete size_t range without multiplying a
possibly huge gap by ten.
)

\toc

> One wide exchange, then a shrinking gap

For the original [5,3,8,1,9,2,7], the first gap is floor(7×10/13)=5. The pass
compares positions (0,5) and (1,6), swapping values 5 and 2 in the first pair.
The small value jumps five positions left. Each subsequent pass uses

\[
g_{k+1}=\max\left(1,\left\lfloor\frac{10g_k}{13}\right\rfloor\right),\qquad g_0=n.
\]
\alttext(The next gap is the greater of one and the integer floor of ten times the current gap divided by thirteen. The initial gap equals the input length.)

The gap is shrunk before scanning, and pairs are visited in ascending left-index
order. One pass costs n−g key comparisons. A zero-swap pass with g>1 does not
stop the algorithm: smaller gaps still have work to do. Only a zero-swap gap-one
scan certifies the complete sequence as sorted. This is the plain 10/13 schedule;
it does not replace a computed gap of 9 or 10 by 11.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/comb_gap_exchange.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::comb_sort_trace({5,3,8,1,9,2,7});
  if(t.work.output!=std::vector<int>{1,2,3,5,7,8,9} || t.work.key_comparisons!=23 || t.work.swaps!=6)return 1;
  std::print("| pass | actual gap | key comparisons | swaps | actual values after pass |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.passes.size();++i) {
    const auto& p=t.passes[i];
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",i+1,p.gap,p.key_comparisons,p.swaps,p.values);
  }
  std::print("\nActual comparisons {}; swaps {}; complete passes {}; gap-one passes {}.\n",t.work.key_comparisons,t.work.swaps,t.work.pass_count,t.work.gap_one_passes);
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(65,1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=1.25;box.height=1.15;box.font_size=17;
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.input.size();++i) {
    box.fill=(i==0 || i==5)?dm::graphics::RGB{255,237,213}:dm::graphics::RGB{239,246,255};
    d.node(std::format("in{}",i),{1.6*i,0},std::format("index {}\n{}",i,t.input[i]),box);
    box.fill=(i==0 || i==5)?dm::graphics::RGB{220,252,231}:dm::graphics::RGB{239,246,255};
    d.node(std::format("after{}",i),{1.6*i,-2},std::format("index {}\n{}",i,t.passes[0].values[i]),box);
  }
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke jump;jump.arrow=true;jump.color={234,88,12};jump.width=3;
  d.path({{8,.75},{8,1.4},{0,1.4},{0,.75}},jump)
   .text({4,1.95},"Value 2 jumps five positions left at gap 5",20)
   .text({4.8,3.1},"Actual first pass: compare (0,5), then (1,6)",23)
   .text({4.8,-3.6},std::format("After the actual gap-5 pass: {}",t.passes[0].values),19)
   .save_svg("build/comb_gap_exchange.svg");
}
```
